msgid "The C interface JSON file"
msgstr "C 接口 JSON 文件"

msgid ""
"The ``gdextension_interface.json`` file is the \"source of truth\" for the C "
"API that Godot uses to communicate with GDExtensions."
msgstr ""
"``gdextension_interface.json`` 文件是 Godot 用于与 GDExtensions 通信的 C API "
"的“真理之源”。"

msgid ""
"You can use the Godot executable to dump the file by using the following "
"command:"
msgstr "你可以通过以下命令，使用 Godot 可执行文件来转储文件："

msgid ""
"This file is intended to be used by GDExtension language bindings to "
"generate code for using this API in whatever form makes the most sense for "
"that language."
msgstr ""
"此文件旨在供 GDExtension 语言绑定使用，以生成使用此 API 的代码，并以最适合该"
"语言的形式呈现。"

msgid ""
"This is not to be confused with the ``extension_api.json``, which is also "
"used by GDExtension language bindings, and contains information about the "
"classes and methods that are exposed by Godot. The "
"``gdextension_interface.json`` is more low-level, and is used to interact "
"with those higher-level classes and methods."
msgstr ""
"请勿将此文件与 ``extension_api.json`` 混淆，后者也由 GDExtension 语言绑定使"
"用，其中包含 Godot 公开的类和方法的相关信息。 ``gdextension_interface.json`` "
"更底层 ，用于与这些更高级别的类和方法进行交互。"

msgid ""
"For languages that can be extended via C, or provide tools for interacting "
"with C code, it's also possible to use the Godot executable to dump a "
"generated C header file:"
msgstr ""
"对于可以通过 C 语言扩展或提供与 C 代码交互工具的语言，也可以使用 Godot 可执行"
"文件来转储生成的 C 语言的头文件："

msgid ""
"The header file is compatible with earlier versions of the header file that "
"were included with Godot 4.5 and earlier, which means it preserves some "
"typos in names in order to ensure compatibility."
msgstr ""
"该头文件与 Godot 4.5 及更早版本中所包含的头文件兼容，这意味着它保留了一些名称"
"拼写错误以确保兼容性 。"

msgid ""
"The goal of this page is to explain the JSON format for the GDExtension "
"language bindings that would like to do their own code generation from the "
"JSON."
msgstr ""
"本页的目标是解释 GDExtension 语言绑定的 JSON 格式，以便它们能够根据 JSON 生成"
"自己的代码。"

msgid "Overall structure"
msgstr "整体结构"

msgid "The JSON file is broken up into 3 sections:"
msgstr "JSON 文件分为 3 个部分："

msgid ""
"The header, which includes some miscellaneous information at the top-level "
"of the JSON file."
msgstr "头部信息，其中包含 JSON 文件顶层的一些杂项信息。"

msgid ""
"The ``types`` key, which defines all the types used in the GDExtension "
"interface."
msgstr "``types`` 键定义了 GDExtension 接口中使用的所有类型。"

msgid ""
"The ``interface`` key, which defines all the function pointers that can be "
"loaded via the ``GDExtensionInterfaceGetProcAddress`` function pointer, "
"which is passed to all GDExtensions when they are loaded."
msgstr ""
"``interface`` 键定义了所有可以通过 ``GDExtensionInterfaceGetProcAddress`` 函"
"数指针加载的函数指针，该函数指针会在加载所有 GDExtension 时传递给它们。"

msgid ""
"There is a complete `JSON schema <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/"
"master/core/extension/gdextension_interface.schema.json>`__ included in "
"Godot's source code."
msgstr ""
"Godot 的源代码中包含一个完整的 `JSON schema <https://github.com/godotengine/"
"godot/blob/master/core/extension/gdextension_interface.schema.json>`__ 。"

msgid ""
"Even though we may add new types and interface functions with each minor "
"release of Godot, we strive to **never** change them in a backwards "
"incompatible way, or remove them. Every interface function is labeled with "
"the version of Godot it was introduced in (the ``since`` key), so you can "
"always use the latest version of the file, and simply refrain from using "
"anything in versions of Godot that are newer than the version you are "
"targeting."
msgstr ""
"尽管我们可能会在 Godot 的每个小版本更新中添加新的类型和接口函数，但我们力求"
"\\ **绝不**\\ 以不兼容的方式更改或移除它们。每个接口函数都标有引入它的 Godot "
"版本（\\ ``since`` 键），因此你可以始终使用文件的最新版本，只需避免使用比目标"
"版本更新的 Godot 版本中的任何内容即可。"

msgid "Header"
msgstr "头部信息"

msgid ""
"The \"header\" is made up of 3 miscellaneous keys at the top-level of the "
"file:"
msgstr "文件“头部”由位于文件顶层的 3 个杂项键组成："

msgid ""
"``_copyright``: The standard copyright and license text that Godot includes "
"in all source code files."
msgstr "``_copyright``\\ ：Godot 包含在所有源代码文件中的标准版权和许可文本。"

msgid ""
"``$schema``: Points to the JSON schema relative to this file. It can be "
"useful to place the schema in the same directory, if you're viewing it with "
"a code editor that understands JSON schema."
msgstr ""
"``$schema``\\ ：指向相对于此文件的 JSON 模式。如果你使用支持 JSON 模式的代码"
"编辑器查看此文件，将模式放在同一目录中会很有帮助。"

msgid ""
"``format_version``: An integer for the version of the file format (meaning "
"the schema). Right now, there is only one format version (``1``). If we ever "
"change the file format in an incompatible way, we will increment this "
"number. This *doesn't* reflect the version of the data in the file (so it "
"won't change between Godot versions), only its format. Hopefully, we'll "
"never have to use it, but it allows code generators to error early if they "
"encounter an unexpected value here."
msgstr ""
"``format_version``\\ ：文件格式（即模式）的版本号，以整数形式表示。目前只有一"
"个格式版本（\\ ``1``\\ ）。如果我们以不兼容的方式更改文件格式，我们会递增此数"
"值。此值\\ *不是*\\ 反映文件中数据的版本（因此在 Godot 版本之间不会改变），只"
"是反映其格式。我们希望永远不需要用到它，但它可以让代码生成器在此处遇到意外值"
"时尽早报错。"

msgid "Types"
msgstr "类型"

msgid ""
"The ``types`` section is an array of types that will be used by other types, "
"and the interface functions that will be in the last section."
msgstr ""
"``types`` 部分是一个类型数组，其将被其他类型以及在最后一节出现的接口函数使"
"用。"

msgid ""
"The types should be evaluated in order. Later types may refer to earlier "
"types, but earlier types will not refer to later types."
msgstr ""
"这些类型应当按顺序求值。后面的类型可以引用前面的类型，但前面的类型不能引用后"
"面的类型。"

msgid ""
"There is a small set of built-in types which aren't explicitly listed in the "
"JSON:"
msgstr "有一小部分内置类型没有在 JSON 中明确列出："

msgid "``void``"
msgstr "``void``"

msgid "``int8_t``"
msgstr "``int8_t``"

msgid "``uint8_t``"
msgstr "``uint8_t``"

msgid "``int16_t``"
msgstr "``int16_t``"

msgid "``uint16_t``"
msgstr "``uint16_t``"

msgid "``int32_t``"
msgstr "``int32_t``"

msgid "``uint32_t``"
msgstr "``uint32_t``"

msgid "``int64_t``"
msgstr "``int64_t``"

msgid "``uint64_t``"
msgstr "``uint64_t``"

msgid ""
"``size_t`` (``uint32_t`` on 32-bit architectures, and ``uint64_t`` on 64-bit "
"architectures)"
msgstr ""
"``size_t``\\ （32 位架构为 ``uint32_t``\\ ，64 位架构为 ``uint64_t``\\ ）"

msgid "``char``"
msgstr "``char``"

msgid "``char16_t``"
msgstr "``char16_t``"

msgid "``char32_t``"
msgstr "``char32_t``"

msgid "``wchar_t``"
msgstr "``wchar_t``"

msgid "``float``"
msgstr "``float``"

msgid "``double``"
msgstr "``double``"

msgid "These correspond to their equivalent C types."
msgstr "这些与它们对应的 C 类型相对应。"

msgid "Additionally, types can include modifiers such as:"
msgstr "此外，类型还可以包含以下修饰符："

msgid "``*`` (e.g. ``int8_t*``) to indicate a pointer to the type"
msgstr "``*``\\ （例如 ``int8_t*``\\ ）表示指向该类型的指针"

msgid "``const`` (e.g. ``const int8_t*``) to indicate a const type"
msgstr "``const``\\ （例如 ``const int8_t*``\\ ）表示常量类型"

msgid "Each type defined in the JSON file falls into one of 5 \"kinds\":"
msgstr "在 JSON 文件中定义的每一个类型都属于五种“类别”之一："

msgid "``enum``"
msgstr "``enum``"

msgid "``handle``"
msgstr "``handle``"

msgid "``alias``"
msgstr "``alias``"

msgid "``struct``"
msgstr "``struct``"

msgid "``function``"
msgstr "``function``"

msgid "Regardless of the \"kind\", all types can have the following keys:"
msgstr "无论是何种“类别”，所有的类型均可包含以下键："

msgid "``kind`` (required): The type's \"kind\"."
msgstr "``kind``\\ （必填）：该类型的“类别”。"

msgid ""
"``name`` (required): The name of the type, which could be used as a valid C "
"identifier."
msgstr "``name``\\ （必填）：该类型的名称，可作为有效的 C 标识符。"

msgid ""
"``description``: An array of strings documenting the type, where each string "
"is a line of documentation (this format for ``description`` is used "
"throughout the JSON file)."
msgstr ""
"``description``\\ ：一个描述该类型的字符串数组，每个字符串为文档的一行（此 "
"``description`` 格式在整个 JSON 文件中通用）。"

msgid ""
"``deprecated``: An object with its own keys for the Godot version the type "
"was deprecated in (``since``), a message explaining the deprecation "
"(``message``), and optionally a replacement to use instead (``replacement``)."
msgstr ""
"``deprecated``\\ ：一个包含以下键的对象：该类型被弃用时的 Godot 版本号（\\ "
"``since``\\ ），弃用原因（\\ ``message``\\ ），以及选填的替代项（\\ "
"``replacement``\\ ）。"

msgid "Enums"
msgstr "枚举"

msgid ""
"Enums are 32-bit integers with a fixed set of possible values. In C, they "
"could be represented as an ``enum``."
msgstr ""
"枚举是所有可能取值在固定集合内的 32 位整数。在 C 语言中，它们可以表示为 "
"``enum``\\ 。"

msgid "They have the following keys:"
msgstr "它们有以下键："

msgid ""
"``is_bitfield``: If true, this enum is a bitfield, where the enum values can "
"be bitwise OR'd together. It is false by default."
msgstr ""
"``is_bitfield``\\ ：如果为 true，则此枚举是一个位域，其枚举值可以用位或组合。"
"默认为 false。"

msgid ""
"``values``: The array of fixed values for this enum, each with a ``name``, "
"``value``, and ``description``."
msgstr ""
"``values``\\ ：此枚举的所有固定取值组成的数组。每个取值包含名称（\\ "
"``name``\\ ）、值（\\ ``value``\\ ）以及说明（\\ ``description``\\ ）。"

msgid ""
"An enum should be represented as an ``int32_t``, unless ``is_bitfield`` is "
"true, in which case a ``uint32_t`` should be used."
msgstr ""
"枚举类型应当表示为 ``int32_t``\\ ；但如果 ``is_bitfield`` 为 true，则应使用 "
"``uint32_t``\\ 。"

msgid "Example"
msgstr "示例"

msgid "Handles"
msgstr "句柄"

msgid ""
"Handles are pointers to opaque structs. In C, they could be represented as "
"``void *`` or ``struct{} *``."
msgstr ""
"句柄是指向不透明结构体的指针。在 C 语言中，它们可表示为 ``void *`` 或 "
"``struct{} *`` 。"

msgid ""
"``is_const``: If true, this handle type is to be treated as a \"const "
"pointer\", meaning its internal data will not be changed. It is false by "
"default."
msgstr ""
"``is_const``：如果为 true，则此句柄类型将被视为“常量指针”，意味着其内部数据不"
"会被更改。默认情况下为 false。"

msgid ""
"``is_uninitialized``: If true, this handle type is to be treated as pointing "
"to uninitialized memory (which may be initialized using interface "
"functions). It is false by default."
msgstr ""
"``is_uninitialized``\\\\ ：如果为 true，则此句柄类型应被视为指向未初始化的内"
"存（可以使用接口函数初始化）。默认值为 false。"

msgid ""
"``parent``: The optional name of another handle type, if this handle type is "
"the const or uninitialized version of the parent type. This only makes sense "
"if either ``is_const`` or ``is_uninitialized`` is true."
msgstr ""
"``parent``：选填，父句柄类型的名称，当此句柄类型是父类型的常量或未初始化版本"
"时使用。只有当 ``is_const`` 或 ``is_uninitialized`` 为 true 时，此键才有意"
"义。"

msgid ""
"Handles are the size of pointers on the given architecture (so, 64-bit on "
"x86_64 and 32-bit on x86_32, for example)."
msgstr ""
"句柄的大小与给定架构上的指针大小相同（例如，在 x86_64 上为 64 位，在 x86_32 "
"上为 32 位）。"

msgid "Aliases"
msgstr "别名"

msgid ""
"Aliases are alternative names for a type. In C, they could be represented as "
"a ``typedef``."
msgstr "别名是一种类型的替代名称。在 C 语言中，它可以表示为 ``typedef``\\ 。"

msgid "They have only one additional key:"
msgstr "它们仅有一个额外的键："

msgid ""
"``type``: The type the alias is an alternative name for. It may include "
"modifiers as described above."
msgstr "``type``\\ ：别名所替代的原始类型。它可以包含前文描述的修饰符。"

msgid ""
"These should be represented using the same C type as the type they refer to."
msgstr "它们应当使用与所对应原始类型相同的 C 类型来表示。"

msgid "Structs"
msgstr "结构体"

msgid ""
"Structs represent C ``struct``\\ s (aka a block of memory made up of the "
"given members in order), and should follow all the same layout and alignment "
"rules as C structs."
msgstr ""
"结构体表示 C 的 ``struct``\\ （也就是由给定成员按顺序组成的一块内存），并且应"
"遵循所有与 C 结构体相同的布局和对齐规则。"

msgid ""
"``members``: An array of objects which have a ``name``, ``type`` (which may "
"include modifiers), and ``description``."
msgstr ""
"``members``：一个对象数组，其中每个对象包含 ``name`` 、 ``type`` （可能包含修"
"饰符）和 ``description`` 。"

msgid "Functions"
msgstr "函数"

msgid ""
"Functions represent C function pointer types, with a list of arguments and a "
"return type, and should follow the same size and alignment requirements as C "
"function pointers."
msgstr ""
"函数表示 C 函数指针类型，包含参数列表和返回类型，且应遵循与 C 函数指针相同的"
"大小和对齐要求。"

msgid "They have the following members:"
msgstr "它们含有如下成员："

msgid ""
"``return_value``: An object which has a ``type`` (which may include "
"modifiers) and ``description``. If the function has no return value, this "
"will be omitted."
msgstr ""
"``return_value``：一个包含 ``type`` （可能包含修饰符）和 ``description`` 的对"
"象。如果函数没有返回值，则省略此字段。"

msgid ""
"``arguments`` (required): An array of function arguments which each has a "
"``type`` (which may include modifiers), ``name``, and ``description``."
msgstr ""
"``arguments`` （必需）：一个函数参数数组，其中每个参数包含 ``type`` （可能包"
"含修饰符）、 ``name`` 和 ``description`` 。"

msgid "Interface"
msgstr "接口"

msgid ""
"The ``interface`` section of the JSON file is the list of interface "
"functions, which can be loaded by ``name`` using the "
"``GDExtensionInterfaceGetProcAddress`` function pointer, which is passed to "
"all GDExtensions when they are loaded."
msgstr ""
"JSON 文件中的 ``interface`` 部分是接口函数列表，可通过在加载时传入所有 "
"GDExtension 的 ``GDExtensionInterfaceGetProcAddress`` 函数指针，按 ``name`` "
"加载这些函数。"

msgid ""
"Interface functions have some of the same keys as types, including ``name`` "
"(required), ``deprecated``, and ``description``."
msgstr ""
"接口函数具有与类型相同的部分键，包括 ``name`` （必需）、 ``deprecated`` 和 "
"``description`` 。"

msgid ""
"And they also have ``return_value`` and ``arguments`` (required) that have "
"the same format as the equivalent keys on function types (as described in "
"the previous section)."
msgstr ""
"它们还具有 ``return_value`` 和 ``arguments`` （必需），其格式与函数类型中对应"
"键的格式相同（如上一节所述）。"

msgid "There are only a handful of unique keys:"
msgstr "只有少量的几个唯一键："

msgid ""
"``since`` (required): The Godot version that introduced this interface "
"function."
msgstr "``since`` （必需）：引入此接口函数的 Godot 版本。"

msgid ""
"``see``: An array of strings describing external references with more "
"information, for example, names of classes or functions in the Godot source "
"code, or URLs pointing to documentation."
msgstr ""
"``see`` ：一个字符串数组，用于描述包含更多信息的外部引用，例如 Godot 源代码中"
"的类名或函数名，或指向文档的 URL。"

msgid ""
"``legacy_type_name``: The legacy name used for the function pointer type in "
"the header generated by Godot, when the legacy name doesn't match the "
"pattern used for these type names. This field only exists so that we can "
"generate the header in a way that is backwards compatible with the header "
"from Godot 4.5 or earlier, and it shouldn't be used unless you also need to "
"maintain compatibility with the old header."
msgstr ""
"``legacy_type_name`` ：当旧版名称与函数指针类型的命名规则不一致时，该字段用于"
"指定 Godot 生成的头文件中该函数指针类型所使用的旧版名称。此字段的存在仅是为了"
"以向后兼容的方式生成头文件，使其与 Godot 4.5 或更早版本的头文件保持兼容；除非"
"您同样需要维持对旧版头文件的兼容性，否则不应使用此字段。"
